B.bnb=new A.hK("misfire","Misfire","Watches every cylinder for misfires \u2013 when the fuel in a cylinder doesn\u2019t burn properly.","On most cars it runs continuously while you drive, so it\u2019s usually ready within minutes.",null)
B.bn_=new A.hK("fuel_system","Fuel system","Checks the engine can keep its air\u2013fuel mixture right, with fuel trims inside their limits.","Runs continuously and is normally ready after a short drive once the engine is warm.",null)
B.bn1=new A.hK("components","Comprehensive components","Checks the engine\u2019s sensors and other parts for wiring faults and for readings that are out of range or don\u2019t make sense.","Runs continuously and is usually ready almost straight away.",null)
B.bn5=new A.hK("catalyst","Catalytic converter","Checks the catalytic converter is still cleaning up the exhaust, by comparing the oxygen sensors before and after it.","Needs steady driving at a constant speed with the engine fully warm \u2013 often 10\u201320 minutes on a main road or highway, sometimes over several drives.","Petrol engines")
B.bn7=new A.hK("heated_catalyst","Heated catalyst","Checks the electric heater that warms some catalytic converters quickly after a cold start. Few cars have one.","Needs a cold start followed by a normal drive.","Petrol engines")
B.bmZ=new A.hK("evap_system","Evaporative system","Checks the fuel tank, cap and vapour lines for leaks, so petrol vapour doesn\u2019t escape into the air.","Often the slowest to finish. Many cars only run it after sitting for several hours or overnight, with the tank between about a quarter and three-quarters full and a mild outside temperature \u2013 it can take a week of normal driving.","Petrol engines")
B.bmY=new A.hK("secondary_air","Secondary air system","Checks the pump that blows extra air into the exhaust after a cold start to help the catalytic converter warm up. Only some cars have one.","Needs a cold start, usually after the car has sat for several hours.","Petrol engines")
B.bn8=new A.hK("ac_refrigerant","Petrol particulate filter","Checks the filter that traps soot from direct-injection petrol engines. Some older cars used this test slot for air-conditioning refrigerant instead.","Needs normal driving, including some longer trips, for the filter to be assessed. Only some cars run it.","Petrol engines")
B.bn4=new A.hK("o2_sensor","Oxygen sensors","Checks the oxygen sensors respond quickly and accurately, since the engine relies on them to get the mixture right.","Usually finishes after a warm drive with some steady cruising and a spell of coasting off the accelerator.","Petrol engines")
B.bn6=new A.hK("o2_sensor_heater","Oxygen sensor heaters","Checks the heaters that bring the oxygen sensors up to working temperature quickly after a start.","Usually finishes within a few minutes of driving after a cold start.","Petrol engines")
B.bn3=new A.hK("nmhc_catalyst","NMHC catalyst","Checks the catalyst that cleans unburnt fuel (non-methane hydrocarbons, or NMHC) out of a diesel\u2019s exhaust.","Usually needs a longer drive at a steady speed with the engine fully warm, and can take several trips.","Diesel engines")
B.bna=new A.hK("nox_scr","NOx after-treatment","Checks the system that removes nitrogen oxides (NOx) from a diesel\u2019s exhaust \u2013 usually a catalyst that uses AdBlue, or a NOx trap.","Needs a fully warm engine and exhaust, often on a longer highway drive.","Diesel engines")
B.bn9=new A.hK("boost_pressure","Boost pressure","Checks the turbocharger delivers the boost pressure the engine computer asks for.","Usually finishes after a warm drive that includes some firmer acceleration.","Diesel engines")
B.bmX=new A.hK("exhaust_gas_sensor","Exhaust gas sensors","Checks the oxygen and NOx sensors in a diesel\u2019s exhaust, which the emissions systems rely on.","Usually finishes after a warm drive that includes some coasting off the accelerator.","Diesel engines")
B.bn2=new A.hK("pm_filter","Diesel particulate filter","Checks the diesel particulate filter (DPF), which traps soot, and the sensor that measures how full it is.","Often needs a longer run at highway speed so the filter can burn off its soot. Lots of short trips can stop it finishing.","Diesel engines")
B.bn0=new A.hK("egr_vvt","EGR and variable valve timing","Checks the exhaust gas recirculation (EGR) valve and, on some engines, the variable valve timing system \u2013 both help with emissions, economy and power.","Often needs a drive that includes cruising and slowing down off the accelerator, sometimes over several trips.",null)
